body: "## Exact-head hosted observation\n\nAt main `131dc3a6ff15ab3d127611f041b5385e5d54257e`, package `pm-vcs@2026.11.2`, [Node 22 job 126381876577](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41771461126/job/126381876577) finished failed on 2026-11-04 at 06:57 UTC. The runner selected Node v22.23.4 and Bun 1.3.14.\n\nThe first full npm release gate succeeded: its two test groups reported 2,537/2,537 and 1,939/1,939 passes, no failures/skips, followed by 100% coverage across all four metrics and the remaining acceptance/quality steps. The subsequent `bun run release:check` invokes the Node release-suite runner through coverage. That phase reported 2,537 tests, 2,536 passes, one failure and zero skips.\n\nThe sole failing case was `test/bisect.test.ts:494`, “a walk killed mid-flight resumes from the durable state without retesting judged changes”. It failed during fixture package installation at line 507, before spawning the process to be killed:\n\n```text\nnpm pack failed: npm pack: skipping merge-driver install during artifact creation\ninstallPackedExtension (scripts/pm-environment.ts:105:36)\n```\n\n[Exact test](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/131dc3a6ff15ab3d127611f041b5385e5d54257e/test/bisect.test.ts#L494-L513) and [installer](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/131dc3a6ff15ab3d127611f041b5385e5d54257e/scripts/pm-environment.ts#L90-L112) confirm that order. The installer uses `spawnSync` for `npm pack --silent --pack-destination <owned-temp-dir>`, refuses any nonzero/null status, and formats an error from result.error or stderr/stdout. The retained diagnostic does not expose the exit status or signal; the skip notice alone is not a diagnosed failure cause.\n\nThe subsequent coverage report also failed its unchanged 100% thresholds (aggregate 99.93% statements/lines, 99.68% branches, 99.92% functions). This report does not assert that the single fixture failure explains every coverage shortfall. Full raw coverage remains in the [job artifact](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41771461126/artifacts/13302332631).\n\n## Expected, actual, impact and limits\n\nThe [CI workflow](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/131dc3a6ff15ab3d127611f041b5385e5d54257e/.github/workflows/ci.yml) requires both complete gates. The [canonical bisect acceptance](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/131dc3a6ff15ab3d127611f041b5385e5d54257e/.agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-p7bisect.toon) requires interrupted execution to remain explicit and resumable.\n\nExpected: package setup succeeds, the crash/resume assertion actually runs, and exact-head release gates retain full assertions and coverage. Actual: fixture packaging stops the crash/resume case and blocks Node 22 certification. This is a hosted CI/harness failure, not proof that production bisect loses data. No independent local rerun, root-cause attribution, repeatability or Node 26 equivalence is claimed.\n\nAt final cleanup the runner still reported about 90,463,156 KiB free and 6% inode use. No ENOSPC is reported for this failure, so it is not established as recurrence of #154. Likewise this is not the ENOTEMPTY teardown in #151, or the native erasure/recovery assertions in #158. The existing `pm-vcs-testenv` item concerns ambient agent provenance/instrumentation, not this pack outcome.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n\n- Capture bounded, sanitized child exit status, signal, spawn error and relevant npm stdout/stderr on this failure; establish the actual cause before changing runtime behavior.\n- Preserve owned temporary-directory cleanup and unchanged semantic assertions, timeouts, coverage thresholds and source inventory.\n- Add a regression tied to the diagnosed packing failure, including a control proving the real crash/resume assertions execute rather than skipping setup.\n- Obtain complete successful npm and Bun-invoked release gates on the same final immutable head, with explicit test and coverage receipts. Keep certification incomplete until then.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nRead all 174 all-status GitHub issue/PR records (100 + 74, unique numbers) and all 161 canonical issue/task/chore/feature records at the tested SHA, including the bisect, test-environment and pack owners; refreshed latest GitHub records immediately before filing. No matching pack-setup CI owner found. Existing broader certification and historical failures remain separate.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-04T09:41:24Z)\n>\n> Root cause found and reproduced; the fix is in #178 ([pm-vcs-v5bg](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-vcs-v5bg.toon)).\n> \n> **Cause.** `npm pack` runs `prepack` (`npm run build` = `tsc`), which truncates and rewrites `dist/`. The release suite runs up to four test files at once. When one file's `tsc` rewrites `dist/` while another file's `npm pack` is archiving it, node-tar fails with `npm error code EOF` / `syscall read` / `encountered unexpected EOF` on a `dist/` file. `--silent` suppressed that error, so the diagnostic kept only the prepare script's harmless skip notice. The exit status was 1, not a signal: on a timeout `result.error` would have been set.\n> \n> **Reproduction.** Four workers each ran 15 staggered `npm pack --loglevel error` calls in one checkout. 3 of 60 and then 5 of 60 failed, on `dist/engine/lifecycle.js`, `dist/ledger.js` and `dist/engine/destruction.js.map`.\n> \n> **Second hosted occurrence.** #177's run [41790449958](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41790449958/job/126442337073), job `test (26)`, failed the same way in a different test: `checkpoints.test.ts:322`, \"installed CLI attaches and inspects JSON and TOON…\". Its coverage summary showed the same aggregate, 99.93% statements and lines and 99.68% branches. So in both runs the shortfall comes with the one failed packed-install test. #178's CI will confirm 100% once the race is gone.\n> \n> **Fix (#178).**\n> - Pack with `--ignore-scripts`, as `composition-consumer.test.ts` and `verify-pack-privacy.ts` already do. Every runner builds first.\n> - Use `--loglevel=error` instead of `--silent`.\n> - Add a regression test: a real pack must leave every `dist/` mtime unchanged. It fails with the old arguments restored.\n> \n> With the new arguments, 60 of 60 staggered concurrent packs succeed.\n>"
